INT. NIGHT BUS - ROUTE N9 - NIGHT

Rain on the windows. The bus is a lit aquarium gliding through a dark city. Neon smears past. In the back row, two teenagers share a bag of chips and a single, furious whisper.

Lucia, 30s, in a rumpled bridesmaid dress and trainers, sits with a bouquet she's clearly been dragging around for hours. She sneezes. The bouquet shakes. A petal lands on her phone.

The doors HISS. Katya, 30s, also in a bridesmaid dress, the same hideous mint green, climbs aboard, drenched, holding her heels in one hand.

They see each other. Freeze.

LUCIA
You.

KATYA
No.

LUCIA
You're wearing it.

KATYA
(sitting across from her)
Everyone's wearing it. It's a bridal party. That's the horror of it.

The bus lurches. Katya slides, grabs a pole, and the heels go flying. One hits the driver's screen with a THUNK.

DRIVER (V.O.)
(over the intercom, bored)
Please keep all footwear to yourselves, ladies.

KATYA
(to the ceiling)
Sorry!

Lucia laughs despite herself. Katya laughs too. They both stop at once.

LUCIA
She's still furious with you, you know. She's saying you ruined the cake.

KATYA
She is saying I ruined the cake? She's the one who told me to hold it.

LUCIA
She's saying she didn't mean while you were dancing.

KATYA
She is not allowed to say that. She's the one who taught me the dance.

Winston, 20s, in a delivery jacket, steps on at the next stop with an enormous pizza box, tags in with a beep, and sits down between them without a word. The two women look at each other across him, then at the box.

WINSTON
(opening it, sheepish)
It's wrong order. It's pineapple. I'm not allowed to take it back.

Lucia and Katya both reach for a slice at the same moment. Their hands collide. Both gasp.

LUCIA
She said she'd kill me.

KATYA
She said she'd kill me.

WINSTON
Who did?

They answer together.

LUCIA AND KATYA
The bride.

Winston nods slowly, takes the slice, and offers the box to the teenagers behind him, who snatch it.

The bus slows. The screen over the driver flickers: NEXT STOP: THE FUTURE. The three of them look up.

DRIVER (V.O.)
Sorry about that. Software update.

The doors HISS open on a street that is bright, white, and absolutely silent.

KATYA
Is that normal?

WINSTON
(chewing)
I've seen worse.

Lucia stands. Offers her the bouquet.

LUCIA
Come on. Let's go find out.
